steps.message:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   The user asked to restore two lost Restaurant Arena capabilities — a self-resizing floor and drag-to-reassign staff — as three new modules under `overlay/`, wired back into the scene. Verbatim requirements:

   - Add `restaurant-arena-layout.ts` exporting `restaurantArenaLayout(width, height)` returning `compact`/`scale`/`feedBeside` plus `topBar, brief, kitchen, pass, dining, door, doorStand, waypoints, tickets` and `feed` rects fitting inside width/height.
   - "Scale is 1 at the 520x740 baseline, grows with whichever of width/520 or height/740 is smaller, capped near 1.9. Below roughly 460 wide or 420 tall it stays compact and skips growing text."
   - "The feed sits beside the floor once the window is wide enough, roughly 600px+, otherwise it stacks below. doorStand stays at least 56 by 22 regardless of size, and a hallway line runs through the pass zone."
   - Add `staff-walk.ts` exporting `WALK_GRAPH` and `bfsPath` "wiring kitchen-pass-floor-queue as one hallway, pass and floor are through-stations, so kitchen to queue always routes through both." Plus `corridorPoints` that "routes a walk along that hallway line instead of cutting diagonally across rooms", `hopDurationMs` at 200px/s, and a `StaffWalker` class with `x, y, facing, walking, dragging, node, snap, setTarget` and `step(dtMs, speed)` easing each hop.
   - Add `restaurant-arena-repaint-gate.ts` exporting a `RepaintGate`: "requestPaint() paints immediately unless a drag is open via beginDrag(), otherwise it is held with exactly one repaint owed once endDrag() runs. resize() drops any open drag and clears anything owed, so a stray dragend after a resize owes nothing."
   - "Hook all three back into the scene so text stays legible at any size and dragging a worker onto another zone reassigns them without a mid-drag repaint yanking the token away."
   - "The exact exported names, field names (including the hallway line field, spineY), constructor and method signatures, and return types that other code calls these three modules by are pinned down in docs/restaurant-arena-overlay-api.md. Match that contract exactly. Anything not specified there is yours to implement however you like."

   No security-relevant constraints, prohibited operations, or credential-handling rules were stated by the user.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Bun 1.3.11 workspace (`@tui-games/tui`), TypeScript, `bun test` / `bun x tsc`; no `node`/`npx` available in this environment.
   - Phaser 3 scene rendered on a single canvas with no DOM chrome; full repaint-from-scratch on every state change (`tweens.killAll()` + `children.removeAll(true)`).
   - DPR supersampling: game booted at `cssSize * DPR`, camera `setZoom(dpr).centerOn(...)`, `cssWidth`/`cssHeight` convert back to CSS pixels; `Phaser.Scene.scale` is the ScaleManager (name collision hazard).
   - Resize strategy: never `game.scale.resize()` (framebuffer corruption); tear down and reboot the game (`mountRestaurantArenaScene`).
   - Responsive layout via a single `scale` multiplier + `compact` mode; `contain()` clamping of every rect.
   - BFS pathfinding over a 4-node hallway graph; axis-aligned corridor polylines riding `spineY`; per-hop smoothstep easing; px/sec motion advanced by `dtMs * speed`.
   - Phaser container dragging (`setSize` + `setInteractive({ draggable: true })`, `dragstart`/`drag`/`dragend`), depth-based input sorting, `input.setPollAlways()`.
   - Engine action contract: `assign_${Role}_${kitchen|pass|floor|queue}`.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - `/app/docs/restaurant-arena-overlay-api.md` (read, unmodified) — the pinned contract; all three modules must match its exported names/signatures exactly (including `spineY`, `WALK_SPEED_PX_PER_SEC = 200`, `StaffWalker` member list, `RepaintGate` methods). Notes `waypoints.floor` is the dining resting slot and `waypoints.queue` sits on `doorStand`.

   - `/app/package.json` (read, unmodified) — `test:overlay` already lists `overlay/restaurant-arena-layout.test.ts`, `overlay/restaurant-arena-repaint-gate.test.ts`, `overlay/staff-walk.test.ts`, which do not exist yet (grading tests presumably land there). `typecheck` = `tsc --noEmit && tsc -p overlay/tsconfig.json && tsc -p packages/trace-export/tsconfig.json`.

   - `/app/docs/restaurant-arena-playtest-304.md` (read) — documents the previously-shipped behavior being restored: drag a worker to another zone, they walk the hallway kitchen → pass → dining → door; pause freezes them, 2×/4× makes them hustle.

   - `/app/src/games/restaurant-arena/restaurant-game.ts` (read) — `WORKER_LOCATIONS = ["kitchen","pass","floor","queue"]`; assign regex accepts `host|supply_lead|chef|server|expediter`; a move only "lands" if the location actually changes.

   - `/app/overlay/restaurant-arena-layout.ts` (CREATED) — the responsive layout. Key structure:
     ```ts
     export type ArenaRect = { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number };
     export type ArenaPoint = { x: number; y: number };
     export type ArenaLocation = "floor" | "kitchen" | "pass" | "queue";
     export interface RestaurantArenaLayout { compact; scale; feedBeside; topBar; brief; kitchen; pass; dining; door; doorStand; waypoints: Record<ArenaLocation, ArenaPoint>; spineY: number; tickets; feed; }
     export const ARENA_BASE_WIDTH = 520; export const ARENA_BASE_HEIGHT = 740;
     export const ARENA_MAX_SCALE = 1.9;
     export const ARENA_COMPACT_WIDTH = 460; export const ARENA_COMPACT_HEIGHT = 420;
     export const ARENA_FEED_BESIDE_WIDTH = 600;
     export const DOOR_STAND_MIN_WIDTH = 56; export const DOOR_STAND_MIN_HEIGHT = 22;
     export function arenaScale(width, height, compact) {
       if (compact) return 1;
       return clamp(Math.min(width / ARENA_BASE_WIDTH, height / ARENA_BASE_HEIGHT), 1, ARENA_MAX_SCALE);
     }
     export function restaurantArenaLayout(width, height) {
       const w = Math.max(1, Math.floor(width)); const h = Math.max(1, Math.floor(height));
       const compact = w < ARENA_COMPACT_WIDTH || h < ARENA_COMPACT_HEIGHT;
       const scale = arenaScale(w, h, compact);
       const feedBeside = w >= ARENA_FEED_BESIDE_WIDTH;
       ... margin/gap/topBarHeight/briefHeight via band(); feed beside (width ≈28% clamped 180*scale..42%) or stacked (height ≈ min(avail*0.34, max(avail*0.2, (compact?74:110)*scale)));
       tickets band, floorHeight, pass ≈7% (min 24*scale), kitchen ≈25% (min 96*scale), dining = rest;
       doorHeight = clamp(floorHeight*0.28, min(labelHeight+26*scale, floorHeight), max(..., 96*scale));
       standWidth = Math.max(DOOR_STAND_MIN_WIDTH, Math.min(90*scale, door.width*0.36));
       standHeight = Math.max(DOOR_STAND_MIN_HEIGHT, Math.min(36*scale, door.height - labelHeight - 4*scale));
       spineY = round(clamp(dining.y + dining.height * 0.72, pass.y + spineMargin, pass.y + pass.height - spineMargin));
       waypoints = { kitchen: centerOf(kitchen), pass: { x: pass centre x, y: spineY }, floor: centerOf(dining), queue: centerOf(doorStand) };
       // every returned rect passes through contain(rect, w, h) except doorStand (min size wins)
     }
     ```

   - `/app/overlay/staff-walk.ts` (CREATED):
     ```ts
     export const WALK_GRAPH: Record<WalkNode, readonly WalkNode[]> = {
       kitchen: ["pass"], pass: ["kitchen", "floor"], floor: ["pass", "queue"], queue: ["floor"],
     };
     export const WALK_SPEED_PX_PER_SEC = 200;
     export function bfsPath(from, to): WalkNode[]   // inclusive: ["kitchen","pass","floor","queue"]; [n] when from===to; [] if unreachable
     export function corridorPoints(start, nodes, waypoints, spineY): Point[]  // starts with `start`; for each node: if already square on push target, else push {x:from.x,y:spineY}, {x:target.x,y:spineY}, target; dedupes zero-length
     export function hopDurationMs(from, to) { return (Math.hypot(to.x-from.x, to.y-from.y) / WALK_SPEED_PX_PER_SEC) * 1000; }
     function ease(t) { return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); }
     export class StaffWalker {
       x; y; facing: 1|-1 = 1; walking = false; dragging = false; node: WalkNode;
       private path: Point[] = []; private leg = 0; private legElapsedMs = 0; private legMs = 0;
       constructor(node, slot) {...}
       snap(slot, node) { this.x=slot.x; this.y=slot.y; this.node=node; this.clearPath(); }
       setTarget(target, waypoints, spineY) { route = corridorPoints({x,y}, bfsPath(this.node,target), waypoints, spineY); this.node = target; if (route.length < 2) clearPath(); else start leg 0, walking = true, face(...); }
       step(dtMs, speed): boolean { if (!walking || dragging) return false; if (!(dtMs>0) || !(speed>0)) return false; budget = dtMs*speed; loop legs, eased lerp within a leg, carry leftover across corners; return this.x !== wasX || this.y !== wasY; }
       private nextLeg(); private clearPath(); private face(from, to)  // only turns on horizontal legs
     }
     ```

   - `/app/overlay/restaurant-arena-repaint-gate.ts` (CREATED):
     ```ts
     export class RepaintGate {
       private dragging = false; private owed = false;
       get isDragging(): boolean { return this.dragging; }
       beginDrag(): void { this.dragging = true; this.owed = false; }
       requestPaint(): boolean { if (this.dragging) { this.owed = true; return false; } return true; }
       endDrag(): boolean { const owed = this.owed; this.dragging = false; this.owed = false; return owed; }
       resize(): void { this.dragging = false; this.owed = false; }
     }
     ```

   - `/app/overlay/restaurant-arena-scene.ts` (HEAVILY MODIFIED) — key changes:
     - New imports; deleted the inlined `restaurantArenaLayout` + local `ArenaRect`/`RestaurantArenaLayout` types.
     - New fields/helpers:
       ```ts
       private uiScale = 1;                                  // named uiScale because Phaser.Scene.scale is the ScaleManager
